## Conventions
- Match existing code style
- Server actions for all mutations
- Ask before adding dependencies
- Keep prd.md updated with general build progress and progress.md updated with implementation details

## Supabase keys (non-negotiable)
- New publishable + secret keys, not legacy `anon` / `service_role`.
- Client uses `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` only; `SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY` is server-only and never `NEXT_PUBLIC_`-prefixed.

## Security non-negotiables
- `@upenn.edu` gate enforced server-side at the auth boundary; client checks are cosmetic.
- Supabase secret key and OpenRouter key never reach the client — all AI calls and secret-key DB ops are server-side.
- RLS on every table, default-deny.
- AI dietary/allergen tags are never authoritative — always AI-suggested + user-confirmed.

## Secrets
- Never read .env.local or any .env.* file with real values.
- Refer to .env.example for required environment variables.
- If you need an env var's value, ask me.

